  "id": "11924822",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "tribus Arnensis",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/tribus"
  ],
  "details": "<p>An inscription (<em>CIL</em> XI 3303 = <em>ILS</em> 154) from Forum Clodii records the name of <em>tribus Arnensis</em>. Providing instructions for celebrating the birthdays of the Imperial house of the Iulio-Claudians, the text names a <em>duumvir</em> of this tribe (Caius Acceius Rufus Lutatius).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Arnensis was one of the later rural tribes of Rome, which was established in 387 B.C.",
  "reprPoint": [
    12.9235265,
    42.270857166666666
  ],
